# Cloudflare Pages header rules, copied verbatim into the deployment root.
#
# Pages resolves MIME types from a fixed extension table, and `.webmanifest` is
# not in it: the file ships with no Content-Type at all, while Pages also sends
# `x-content-type-options: nosniff`. Chrome then refuses to read the manifest,
# so "Install app" never gets the name, icons or colours below it. Declaring the
# type here is the whole fix; `_headers` is not part of the precached shell.

/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
